From 71171f4fcd819e6cf3a19de8613e42dc23a21456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: andrewrpope <andrew.pope@morsemicro.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 08:48:43 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] DPP PB: Increase dwell on scan retry

In d31e7220895f, a retry scan was added to increase DPP PB
reliability. Active scans dwell on-channel following the device's
defaults, which can range from 30 to 60 ms. This is shorter than the
typical 100 TU beacon interval. In highly contested channels, a
station's probe request may collide with other traffic; when this
occurs the station is reliant on receiving a beacon to build a scan
result for that channel. The start of the dwell, however, may not
overlap with a beacon transmission, in which case the station does not
see the target BSS. Running a second scan at the same short dwell does
not materially improve coverage.

Raise the per-channel dwell on the DPP-PB retry scan to 200 TU using
the one-shot wpa_s->next_scan_dwell_duration mechanism. Each channel
visit on the retry spans at least two (default) beacon intervals,
increasing the likelihood of success. The initial PB scan keeps the
default dwell; only the fallback path pays the extra time.

The dwell reaches the kernel as NL80211_ATTR_MEASUREMENT_DURATION and
requires the driver to advertise
WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_SUPPORT_SET_SCAN_DWELL; on drivers without that
capability the attribute is silently dropped and behavior is unchanged.
---
 wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c b/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
index fe15ff837..2b7285b73 100644
--- a/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_DPP3
 #define PUSH_BUTTON_CHIRP_FOREVER_START_DELAY_S (30)
+#define PUSH_BUTTON_RETRY_SCAN_DWELL_TU         (200)
 #endif
 
 static int wpas_dpp_listen_start(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s,
@@ -6113,6 +6114,7 @@ static void wpas_dpp_pb_scan_res_handler(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s,
 	if (wpa_s->dpp_pb_scan_retries < 2) {
 		wpa_s->scan_req = MANUAL_SCAN_REQ;
 		wpa_s->scan_res_handler = wpas_dpp_pb_scan_res_handler;
+		wpa_s->next_scan_dwell_duration = PUSH_BUTTON_RETRY_SCAN_DWELL_TU;
 		wpa_supplicant_cancel_sched_scan(wpa_s);
 		wpa_supplicant_req_scan(wpa_s, 0, 500000);
 		return;
